WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.647
- [Instructor] We are told,
"Select the two fractions

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.120
"that are greater than one."

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.540
So pause this video and
see if you can figure out

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.163
which two of these fractions
are greater than one.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.540
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.750
And so, the main realization here,

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.821
the main thing to pay attention
to is how the numerator

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.330
relates to the denominator.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:28.190
When we are at one, they're
equal to each other.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.290
For example, one is equal to one whole.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.015
I guess you could write
it that way, one oneths.

00:00:34.015 --> 00:00:36.630
Or you could also write it as two halves,

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.768
is also equal to three thirds,

00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:41.030
is also equal to four fourths.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:41.930
We could go on and on.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.450
If you want it in terms of sixths,

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.250
one would be equal to six sixths.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.410
And so, if whatever we have up here

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.445
is larger than the denominator,

00:00:51.445 --> 00:00:53.790
so if we have seven sixths

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:58.630
or if we were to have maybe five fourths.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:01.080
Notice, the numerator is
larger than denominator.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.740
These are all situations
when we are greater than one.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.660
And all the situations where the numerator

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.710
is less than the denominator,
so example one half

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.710
or nine 11ths, or 10 11ths,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.230
these are all situations
where we are less than one.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.330
All of this is less than one.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.770
So let's look over here.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.540
Four is less than six.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.850
Four sixths is less than six sixths.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.310
Remember is the same thing as six sixths.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.040
So this is not greater than one,

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.780
so I would not select that.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.870
Nine fourths, well
that's definitely larger

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.220
than four fourths.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.750
That is greater than one

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.030
and once again our numerator
is larger than our denominator,

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.720
so we know that we are greater than one.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.720
So I will select that one.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.505
And then we see again five halves.

00:01:51.505 --> 00:01:53.582
Two halves is equal to one,

00:01:53.582 --> 00:01:56.660
so five halves is
definitely greater than one.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.310
So I like that one as well.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:00.161
And notice, five is greater than two

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:03.480
and then we are already know
we picked our two choices,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.530
but we can look at the other ones.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:05.754
Seven is less than eight,

00:02:05.754 --> 00:02:08.360
so seven eighths is
less than eight eighths,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:09.850
so this is less than one.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.220
And three thirds, we've
already talked about it,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.320
that's equal to one.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.390
So I like those two choices.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.040
Let's do another example that tackles it

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.328
a little bit of a different way.

00:02:19.328 --> 00:02:22.657
It says, "What, which
fraction could represent

00:02:22.657 --> 00:02:24.450
"Point A on the number line?"

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.320
And Point A is here.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.470
They don't tell us a lot about Point A,

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.030
but all they do tell us by
looking at the number line

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.680
is that Point A is less than one.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.100
So which of these, another
way to think about it,

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.183
is less than one?

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.790
All right, in order for
it to be less than one

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.944
the numerator has to be
less than the denominator.

00:02:43.944 --> 00:02:47.330
Here our numerator is
greater than the denominator.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.830
Seven fourths is definitely
larger than four fourths.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.200
Remember, four fourths is equal to one.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.080
This right over here I could
rewrite as four fourths.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.220
And so, seven fourths is
going to be someplace,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.420
seven fourths is going to
be someplace over there.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.820
So this is definitely not our choice.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.070
Two halves, well once again
that's the same thing as one.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.000
That's right over there.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.590
So that's not our choice.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.083
What about five eighths?

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.383
Well, five eighths,

00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:17.039
the numerator is less
than the denominator.

00:03:17.039 --> 00:03:20.020
Eight eighths is equal to one,

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.340
so that's that point again.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.720
So five eighths would
be to the left of that.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.434
So that could be Point A.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.963
So I like that choice.

